"Stanley  Myrick" <ancientlore@earthlink.net> writes:

> I have had this work before, but now it isn't. I am on windows, and I am 
> editing defaults.nh to make autopickup_exceptions. I've had it to work 
> before when I played Nethack, so I know its possible. But it sure isn't now 
> that I have started back playing. It gives me error boxes for each exception 

It's an optional feature, so probably it was compiled in to the binary
version you used before, but not in the one you use now.
You can check it with the #version (or alt-v) command:
If the feature list includes autopickup_exceptions, it is compiled in,
otherwise it isn't.

> I put in. Maybe I should run the binary again and freshly put in the below 

Starting the same binary again doesn't help in this case, the game has to
be recompiled to change the compile-time options.

The option is defined in the "experimental stuff" section of config.h, so
I suspect all the official versions at the devteam website are compiled
without that option, and you have to either compile it yourself or find
somewhere a version with AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS defined.

